class.description:
The [PathPrefixServer] keeps a table of path prefixes. Each prefix is resolved by logic, a [PathPrefix] or a [Callable], that turns a prefixed path into a real path on the current platform. [FileAccess], [DirAccess], [ResourceLoader], [ResourceSaver] and [method ProjectSettings.globalize_path] resolve every registered prefix.
The engine prefixes are registered first and are locked: [code]res://[/code], [code]user://[/code], [code]uid://[/code], [code]pipe://[/code] and [code]exec://[/code]. [code]exec://[/code] is the folder of the executable in an exported project (on macOS the folder that contains the [code].app[/code] bundle) and the project folder in the editor. It is not available on Android, iOS and the Web.
If [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/path_prefixes/defaults] is enabled, [code]appdata://[/code], [code]config://[/code], [code]cache://[/code] and [code]temp://[/code] are registered at startup for the OS folders of [method OS.get_data_dir], [method OS.get_config_dir], [method OS.get_cache_dir] and [method OS.get_temp_dir]. They can be replaced or removed. On the Web only [code]temp://[/code] is registered, because the other folders are not persistent there.
[method resolve] returns a [PathInfo] with all forms of a path. [method resolve_safe] does the same for untrusted paths from players, mods or the network.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
PathPrefixServer.register_prefix_folder("mods://", "exec://mods")
var file := FileAccess.open("mods://readme.txt", FileAccess.READ)

var info := PathPrefixServer.resolve_safe(player_path, true, ["user://saves/"])
if not info.valid:
	push_error(info.error_message)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
PathPrefixServer.RegisterPrefixFolder("mods://", "exec://mods");
using var file = FileAccess.Open("mods://readme.txt", FileAccess.ModeFlags.Read);

PathInfo info = PathPrefixServer.ResolveSafe(playerPath, true, ["user://saves/"]);
if (!info.Valid)
{
    GD.PushError(info.ErrorMessage);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] [method ProjectSettings.localize_path] does not map OS paths to registered prefixes, so that existing projects keep their behavior. Use [method localize] or [method resolve] for that.
